---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI Monetization Playbook — North End Technology"
  description="Convert AI feature investment into billable, defensible revenue lines."
>
  <section class="playbook-hero section-alt">
    <div class="wrapper">
      <p class="eyebrow">Playbook</p>
      <h1>AI Monetization</h1>
      <p>
        Most AI features ship as a cost center wearing a roadmap slide. This playbook
        turns them into a priced, defensible line item before the next board meeting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrapper playbook-body">
      <h2>Stop shipping AI as a free feature</h2>
      <p>
        If an AI capability is bundled into an existing tier at no incremental price,
        it is a cost center by definition — inference spend rises with usage while
        revenue stays flat. That gap is the first thing a diligence team will flag.
      </p>

      <h2>The monetization sequence</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Meter before you price.</strong> Instrument usage at the unit-of-value level (queries, generations, resolved tickets) before deciding on a packaging model.</li>
        <li><strong>Separate the model cost from the feature price.</strong> Price to the value delivered to the customer, not to the underlying inference bill — the two should not move together.</li>
        <li><strong>Package as an add-on tier, not a base-tier freebie.</strong> A named, priced AI tier is a revenue line a sponsor can model; a bundled feature is not.</li>
        <li><strong>Track margin per AI-adjacent seat.</strong> Report gross margin on AI features separately until it stabilizes — blending it into overall SaaS margin hides the real economics.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What good looks like on the P&amp;L</h2>
      <p>
        A defensible AI monetization line shows rising attach rate, stable or
        improving gross margin per unit, and a clear packaging boundary versus the
        core product. That combination is what converts an AI initiative from a
        product story into a revenue story.
      </p>

      <div class="playbook-cta">
        <a href={`${base}/#contact`} class="btn btn-primary">Discuss this playbook</a>
        <a href={`${base}/#playbooks`} class="back-link">&larr; Back to all playbooks</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
